WEBVTT

NOTE F4: two participants with separate labels. Tom (main speaker: most speaking time) and Grace do several steps differently. Synthetic.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
<v Interviewer>You both run the monthly stock count. Can you take me through it?</v>

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Tom>Sure. The point is the area manager gets accurate figures so the next order isn't wrong. It's the last Sunday of the month, after close.</v>

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Grace>Yeah, if we get it wrong we either run out of oat milk or we're throwing stuff away.</v>

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:44.000
<v Tom>I start by printing the count sheet from the stock spreadsheet, so I've got every item listed by shelf.</v>

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
<v Grace>I don't bother printing it. I count straight into the stock app on the tablet.</v>

6
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Tom>Then I go round shelf by shelf, dry store, fridges, freezer, and write the counts down.</v>

7
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
<v Interviewer>On a scale of one to five, how hard is the counting?</v>

8
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Tom>A four. It's cold, it's late, and the freezer labels are always iced over.</v>

9
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
<v Grace>I'd say a two, honestly. The tablet's quicker.</v>

10
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Tom>Back in the office I type the counts into the spreadsheet. It highlights anything that's way off from what we expected.</v>

11
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:55.000
<v Tom>If something's way off, I go back and recount that item, because nine times out of ten it's me miscounting.</v>

12
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:02.000
<v Grace>I don't recount. I just adjust it and add a note for the manager.</v>

13
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:11.000
<v Tom>Once it all looks right, I email the spreadsheet to the area manager.</v>

14
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:19.000
<v Tom>She reviews the figures and signs it off, usually by Tuesday.</v>

15
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.000
<v Interviewer>How long does it take?</v>

16
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:31.000
<v Tom>About two and a half hours for me, start to finish.</v>

17
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
<v Grace>More like an hour and a half.</v>
